<title>JAPAN: Nissan says demand strong for Stagea.</title>
<headline>Nissan says demand strong for Stagea.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissan Motor Co Ltd received 2,500 domestic orders for its Stagea station wagon in the first week after it went on sale on September 24, a spokeswoman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>When it introduced the Stagea, Nissan said it had a monthly sales target of 5,000 cars.</p>
<p>The Stagea was designed to compete with the Volvo 850 Estate and Mercedes-Benz wagon models, Nissan said.</p>
</text>
